@title  PCSE00120 - boot to the title screen
@game   PCSE00120
@shot-every 400

# WHAT THIS RECIPE PROVES
# ----------------------
# The title boots, links, loads its boot data out of its CPK, brings up its audio graph, and
# reaches the "PRESS ANY BUTTON" title screen. It is the first recipe for this title and it is
# deliberately a BOOT recipe, not a playthrough: nothing past the title screen has been walked.
#
# THE THING THAT COSTS A SESSION IF IT IS NOT WRITTEN DOWN: with NO INPUT AT ALL this title
# sits on a black screen FOREVER, and it looks perfectly healthy while it does - the clock runs
# at 1.00 display periods a frame, audio is produced at 1.00x the clock, its own worker threads
# (model, collision, dungeon) are parked on their condition variables the way an idle frame
# parks them, and the frame issues THREE EMPTY SCENES. A 9,000-frame run of that produces
# fourteen bit-identical black shots. It is waiting for the pad and nothing says so.
#
# HOW TO REPLAY IT, and the knob that is not optional:
#
#   VITASLOP_GXP_LIVE=1 VITASLOP_HEADLESS_RECIPE=<this file> \
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_FRAMES=2100 VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_EVERY=50 \
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_FROM=1900 vitaslop-desktop --game <app> --headless <dir>
#
# WITHOUT `VITASLOP_GXP_LIVE=1` THE FRAME IS BLACK whatever the title is doing: a draw then
# carries no shader blobs, and this title's whole UI is position-only draws whose colour lives
# in the shader, so every one of them is DROPPED for having no colour source. The drop report
# says so on every frame and it still reads as "the guest drew nothing".
#
# WHAT IS NOT ASSERTED, AND WHY
# There is no `@assert` and no `@sig`. No live-state address is known for this title yet, and a
# signature has not been checked for stability across two replays - pinning one that has not
# been measured twice is how a recipe starts failing on a clean tree.
#
# WHAT THE SHOTS ACTUALLY SHOW (re-measured 2026-09-01c, every 200 frames): the boot
# notices (Vox Populi, PSN) up to f2000, the P4G logo splash at f2400, and the yellow title
# screen from about f3200 with "PRESS ANY BUTTON" by f3400. An earlier version of this
# comment said the title screen did not reproduce; it does, and the recipe that goes on
# from it is `new-game.recipe`.
#
# THE PRESSES ARE A MASH, NOT A MINIMAL SEQUENCE. They were found by asking whether the title
# responds to the pad at all, and it does. Which single press first leaves the black screen has
# not been bisected - `explore` over the 300..900 window is the way to narrow it, and doing that
# is what turns this into a tight recipe.
#
# Every press is held 8 frames. The guest samples the pad once per display frame, so a press
# that spans no sample is never observed at all.

300: @section wake
300: cross
308:
360: start
368:
420: circle
428:
480: cross
488:
540: start
548:

900: @section settle
900: cross
908:
960: start
968:

1500: cross
1508:
1560: start
1568:

1900: @section title-screen
2000: @shot title-screen

# @todo Find a live-state address (a menu cursor index is the usual first one) and turn the
# @todo shot judgement above into a real `@assert`.
# @todo Walk past this screen - new game / continue - and extend this into a playable recipe.
